Section 2: Someone's Knocking
What kind of attack does the alert suggest happened?
And the alert is:
{
   description: "DETECTION RULE TRIGGERED",
   severity: "HIGH",
   rule_description: "SUSPICIOUS TEXT IN HTTP REQUEST",
   data: https://www.solvisystems.com/feedback?message=</script>. 
 <script>alert('xss')</script>
}
This indicates XSS, or cross-site scripting. How do we know this? There's a script injected into the previously benign URL. Now, this script won't do much - just show a pop-up with the word 'xss', but it could be someone testing the waters to see what else they may be able to run.

